Fix real upstream gaps (not AXOS features): six functions are called or
referenced from httpd/httpd.c and httpd/web.c with no implementation
anywhere in this Merlin release's source tree, and no GT-AX6000 prebuilt
object provides them either (checked rc/prebuild, libwebapi/prebuild, and
confirmed no libasd.so ships for this model at all, unlike some siblings).
Confirmed via a real build attempt: `make gt-ax6000` fails linking httpd
with "undefined reference to" each of these symbols.

- httpd_reject_url() (httpd.c, handle_request): declared and called
  completely unguarded, with no implementation anywhere. Treated as "never
  reject" (replaced `!httpd_reject_url(url)` with `!0`) — the dispatch now
  behaves exactly as if this url-rejection feature had never been added.

- set_ASUS_NEW_EULA() (web.c, do_set_ASUS_NEW_EULA_cgi): the .cgi handler
  itself exists and is wired up, but the helper it calls does not exist
  anywhere. Reports failure (ret = -1) rather than silently skipping the
  call and falsely claiming success for a EULA acceptance that was never
  actually recorded.

- do_set_ASUS_privacy_policy_cgi(), do_get_ASUS_privacy_policy_cgi() (web.c,
  mime_handlers[] table): declared unconditionally but never defined.
  Guarded out of the table; those two .cgi endpoints are simply unhandled
  (404) rather than failing to link.

- do_set_security_update_cgi(), do_get_security_update_cgi() (web.c,
  mime_handlers[] table): already gated behind
  `#if defined(RTCONFIG_ASD) || defined(RTCONFIG_AHS)`, so ASD/AHS support
  is genuinely on for this build — but neither function has an
  implementation anywhere, and no libasd.so prebuilt exists for GT-AX6000
  at all (compare httpd/../asd/prebuild/, which ships it for e.g.
  RT-AX88U_PRO and GT-AXE11000 but not this model) — a genuine model gap,
  not a build-config mismatch of the kind earlier patches fixed. Left the
  RTCONFIG_ASD/RTCONFIG_AHS guard in place and added `&& 0` alongside it, so
  re-enabling is a one-line change if this model ever gains ASD support.

`git apply --check`-verified against the pinned tag (3004.388.9), applied on
top of 0001-0009. Not yet verified past that point in a completed build —
see docs/build-environment.md and docs/ROADMAP.md.

